---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/docs/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../../components/docs/Code.astro';
import { page } from '../../data/docs-nav';
import { COUNTS, REQUIREMENTS, spell } from '../../data/docs';
import { BETA_TAG, DOWNLOADS, GITHUB_URL, RELEASE_URL } from '../../data/site';

const entry = page('/docs/getting-started/');

const build = `git clone --branch ${BETA_TAG} --depth 1 ${GITHUB_URL}.git
cd Hozz

# Signing lives in a gitignored Local.xcconfig:
echo "DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID" > Local.xcconfig

# Build and install on a connected iPhone:
tools/device-build.sh`;
---

<DocsLayout page={entry}>
  <p>
    Hozz is in <strong>beta</strong>, not released on the App Store or Google Play.
  </p>

  <h2 id="downloads">Downloads</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>iPhone &amp; iPad:</strong> <a href={DOWNLOADS.apple.href}>Join TestFlight</a>.{' '}
      {DOWNLOADS.apple.requires}. Approved external beta v0.1.0 (build 1).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mac:</strong> <a href={DOWNLOADS.mac.href}>Download the DMG</a>.{' '}
      {DOWNLOADS.mac.requires}; universal, signed and notarized. Drag Hozz to Applications,
      eject the disk image, then launch.{' '}
      <a href="/docs/destinations/mac/#authentication">Trusted LAN only</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Android preview:</strong> <a href={DOWNLOADS.android.href}>Download the signed APK</a>.{' '}
      {DOWNLOADS.android.requires}.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a href={RELEASE_URL}>Release notes, checksums and demo</a>.{' '}
    <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/${BETA_TAG}/docs/beta-testing.md`}>Beta testing guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Android: open an archive</h2>
  <p>
    Android cannot read Apple Health. Open a Hozz NDJSON or ZIP archive; archive-only mode
    preserves all types.
  </p>
  <Callout kind="warn" title="Health Connect writes are experimental">
    <p>
      Writes require explicit opt-in and Android 14+. There is no Google Play policy approval.
      Steps, distance, energy and ungrouped sleep remain archive-only. Clinical extraction is disabled.
    </p>
  </Callout>
  <p><a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/${BETA_TAG}/docs/android-beta.md`}>Android beta guide</a>.</p>

  <h2>iPhone and iPad: export Apple Health</h2>

  <h3>1. Give it Health access</h3>

  <p>
    Grant any subset. Change it later in{' '}
    <strong>Settings → Health → Data Access &amp; Devices → Hozz</strong>.
  </p>

  <Callout kind="warn" title="Hozz cannot tell “denied” from “you have none”">
    <p>
      HealthKit reports both cases identically. If expected data is missing, check Health settings.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h3>2. Pick a destination</h3>

  <p>
    Nothing leaves until you add and confirm a destination.
  </p>

  <p>
    On <strong>Automatic</strong>, choose a discovered Mac or one of {spell(COUNTS.presets)} presets.
    Start with <a href="/docs/destinations/folder/">Folder</a> if unsure.
  </p>

  <p>
    Choose its Health types, format and cadence. <strong>Send a test</strong> uses a probe with no
    Health data.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Run the first export</h3>

  <p>
    <strong>Automatic sync</strong> works through history in bounded batches, sharing each pass across selected types.
  </p>

  <p>
    The phone reports completed types; the Mac reports received types and date coverage. Health does
    not reveal totals before reading them, so Hozz cannot give a percentage or estimate.
  </p>

  <Callout kind="note" title="A first backfill looks slow because it is">
    <p>
      iOS grants short background windows. Large archives can take days or weeks.{' '}
      <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Tell slow from stuck.</a>
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <p>
    <strong>Export</strong> builds a historical NDJSON, CSV, JSON, SQLite, Markdown or GPX file.
    Interrupted exports resume from their last durable checkpoint.
  </p>

  <p>Manual export is independent of automatic destinations.</p>

  <h2>Build from source instead</h2>
  <details>
    <summary>Apple builds with Xcode</summary>
    <p>
      Use Xcode {REQUIREMENTS.xcode}+ and{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/yonaskolb/XcodeGen">XcodeGen</a> {REQUIREMENTS.xcodegen} or newer.
    </p>
    <Code caption="Terminal" code={build} />
    <p><code>tools/mac-build.sh</code> builds the Mac app.</p>
    <p>
      Device builds need the App Group <code>group.com.thatcube.Hozz</code> in your developer
      profile. Simulator builds do not.
    </p>
  </details>
</DocsLayout>
